From 6fd1b3f1e78cddcf1b4b201ad3b7b28f47f9afeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bb-machine <ubuntu@bb-machine>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:07:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(queue): recover host-offline waits whose host is
 connected

A row parked on a host-offline wait was retried only by the host's reconnect
event. An attempt that ended without dispatching or rebooking, such as a lost
claim during that reconnect, left the row waiting on a machine that was
already connected, with no later wake.

The periodic idle recovery now rechecks rows parked on host-offline waits for
connected hosts, and a failed automatic attempt logs the row's resulting
state, wait, retry booking and host connection.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
